{"combines": true, "proposition": "Putting the two together shows that the direction of the desorption-kinetics change tracks the direction of the activation-energy change: C10's lower Ea (81.9 vs 130.3 kJ/mol for C0) is consistent with, and offers a mechanistic (Arrhenius-type) basis for, C10's much faster desorption completion times (~11 min vs ~150 min at 300 C; <40 min vs ~450 min at 280 C). Neither observation alone would establish this link: A gives only a derived energy-barrier number with no bearing on actual desorption duration, and B gives only observed times with no stated reason why they differ.", "limits": ["Only two temperatures (280 C, 300 C) are reported for the completion-time comparison, too few to reconstruct an independent Arrhenius relation from B and check it quantitatively against the Ea difference derived in A", "A is a derived kinetic parameter (activation energy, from an Arrhenius-plot slope) while B is a cumulative time-to-completion at fixed temperatures - different kinds of quantity, so the pairing supports agreement in direction only, not a verified magnitude match", "No rate constants or pre-exponential (Arrhenius A-factor) values are given, so it cannot be checked whether the full size of the observed time reduction is accounted for by the lower Ea alone or partly by some other kinetic change"], "not_identifiable": "Whether the observed desorption speedup for C10 is attributable to the lowered activation energy alone or also to a change in the pre-exponential (Arrhenius) factor cannot be separated with the data given, since only Ea values and completion times are reported, not full rate constants", "quantity": {"a": {"kind": "derived kinetic parameter (activation energy)", "what": "Ea in kJ/mol from Arrhenius-plot slopes: 130.3 (C0, slope -15.674) and 81.9 (C10, slope -9.852), panel F8a"}, "b": {"kind": "cumulative time-to-completion (not a rate)", "what": "minutes to reach complete desorption at fixed temperatures: ~150 min (C0) vs ~11 min (C10) at 300 C; ~450 min (C0) vs <40 min (C10) at 280 C, panels F10 and F8b"}}, "labels": {"dependency": "real", "inference_validity": "follows, weakly", "causal_strength": "conditional mechanism"}}